{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cdsp7EvRDfxzpHku67Z3C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GtGhTHTbG2tf3cBahccJqa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7run/B/e7-p02/primary/exec-ws/ea-behavior-statement.md","content":"# E-A behavior statement — e7-p02 (spec-vs-implementation determination over the probe set)\n\nProduced at node `observe-evidence` by reading `package/artifacts/joinspec.md`,\n`package/artifacts/joiner.py`, and `package/artifacts/probes.json`. This artifact is a\nproduct of this session's analysis of joiner.py and MUST NOT be given to the clean-room\nchild (it is excluded from `child/child-input-manifest.json`).\n\n## Artifacts under comparison\n\n- `joinspec.md` states three clauses: (1) items are joined with `\", \"` (comma space);\n  (2) items appear in the order given in the list; (3) an empty list renders as the\n  empty string.\n- `joiner.py` is, in full: `def join_items(items): return \", \".join(reversed(items))`.\n\n## Behaviors exercised by the probes\n\n`probes.json` contains six probes (indices 0–5):\n\n| idx | probe                     | behavior(s) exercised                  | spec-determined output | joiner.py output      |\n|-----|---------------------------|----------------------------------------|------------------------|-----------------------|\n| 0   | `[\"a\"]`                   | singleton rendering                    | `\"a\"`                  | `\"a\"`                 |\n| 1   | `[\"x\", \"y\"]`              | separator; multi-item ordering         | `\"x, y\"`               | `\"y, x\"`              |\n| 2   | `[]`                      | empty-list rendering                   | `\"\"`                   | `\"\"`                  |\n| 3   | `[\"one\", \"two\", \"three\"]` | separator; multi-item ordering (n=3)   | `\"one, two, three\"`    | `\"three, two, one\"`   |\n| 4   | `[\"z\"]`                   | singleton rendering                    | `\"z\"`                  | `\"z\"`                 |\n| 5   | `[\"b\", \"a\"]`              | separator; ordering (order-sensitive content) | `\"b, a\"`        | `\"a, b\"`              |\n\njoiner.py outputs are read directly off the one-line implementation: `\", \".join(reversed(items))`\njoins the items in reversed order with `\", \"`; `reversed` of a singleton is the singleton, and\n`\", \".join` of an empty iterable is `\"\"`.\n\n## Behaviors joinspec.md determines DIFFERENTLY from joiner.py\n\n1. **Ordering of lists with two or more items.** joinspec.md clause 2 (\"Items appear in\n   the order given in the list\") determines the given-order join; joiner.py joins\n   `reversed(items)`, producing the reverse-order join. Divergently determined on every\n   multi-item probe: index 1 (`\"x, y\"` vs `\"y, x\"`), index 3 (`\"one, two, three\"` vs\n   `\"three, two, one\"`), index 5 (`\"b, a\"` vs `\"a, b\"`). This is traceable to explicit\n   spec text (clause 2) and to joiner.py's behavior on probes 1, 3, and 5.\n\nNo other divergently-determined behavior exists on the probe set: the separator\n(clause 1, `\", \"`) matches joiner.py's `\", \"` literal on probes 1/3/5; singleton\nrendering (entailed by clauses 1–2 with a one-element order) matches joiner.py on\nprobes 0/4; empty-list rendering (clause 3, `\"\"`) matches joiner.py on probe 2.\n\n## Behaviors joinspec.md leaves UNDETERMINED\n\nNone. Completeness argument: every probe is a flat list of plain strings, so the only\ndimensions of behavior any probe can exercise are (a) the separator between items,\n(b) the order in which items appear, and (c) the rendering of the empty list — the\noutput of a string-list join is fully characterized by these three. joinspec.md fixes\nall three explicitly (clauses 1, 2, 3). No probe contains non-string items, nested\nlists, or any input outside the spec's stated domain, so no probe reaches behavior on\nwhich the spec is silent.\n\n## E-A conclusion\n\nExactly one probe-exercised behavior is determined differently from joiner.py —\nmulti-item ordering (probes 1, 3, 5) — and no probe-exercised behavior is left\nundetermined. Consequence for E-C (not asserted as verdict here): a faithful\nclean-room implementation of the spec is expected to differ from joiner.py precisely\non the multi-item probes; the verdict itself remains PENDING-INTEGRATION until the\nE-B mechanical comparison exists.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":44227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba8d9a21-6ee2-4515-89b7-4bfd3935816f","uuid":"7279a468-fa31-4350-88af-4461f28ad8bd","timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:35:42.629Z","request_id":"req_011Cdsp7BDfpZkivY72rtiYH"}
