{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdspHzZXTHJr2FNgodWMi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KjPQnCue1tTQb3XS2MfMqA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7run/B/e7-p02/primary/exec-ws/resolution.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"e7-p02\",\n  \"topology_id\": \"isolated-clean-room-author\",\n  \"resolutions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"status\": \"RESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"observe-evidence\",\n      \"answer\": \"Exactly one probe-exercised behavior is determined differently by joinspec.md than by joiner.py: the ordering of lists with two or more items. joinspec.md clause 'Items appear in the order given in the list' mandates the given-order join; joiner.py computes ', '.join(reversed(items)). This diverges on probes 1, 3, and 5 (spec-determined 'x, y' / 'one, two, three' / 'b, a' vs joiner.py's 'y, x' / 'three, two, one' / 'a, b'). No probe-exercised behavior is left undetermined: every probe is a flat list of plain strings, whose join output is fully characterized by separator, order, and the empty-list case, and joinspec.md fixes all three; separator (probes 1/3/5), singleton rendering (probes 0/4), and empty-list rendering (probe 2) are determined identically to joiner.py. Full per-probe traceability and completeness argument in ea-behavior-statement.md.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-1\", \"ev-2\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\n      \"answer\": \"PENDING-INTEGRATION. This session has read joiner.py and the full package, so any implementation it authored would be void under E-B's authorship condition. A clean-room child bundle has been proposed at propose-child (child/): a fresh, terminal Read+Write worker whose input manifest is exactly package/artifacts/joinspec.md and whose deliverable is impl.py exposing join_items(items). The root-executed validate-child / create-child / child-return nodes settle Q2.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-3\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\n      \"answer\": \"PENDING-INTEGRATION. The item-level comparison over all six probes between joiner.py and the clean-room impl.py cannot exist before the child artifact exists. The deterministic comparison rule (fresh copy per call, sorted divergent-index list D) is pre-committed in child/integration-plan.json and is executed at root-executed verify-integration.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-3\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n      \"resolved_by\": \"\",\n      \"answer\": \"PENDING-INTEGRATION. Per its admissibility constraints the verdict may not be asserted from spec-reading or code-reading alone; only PENDING-INTEGRATION is admissible before the E-B comparison exists. The pre-committed rule in child/integration-plan.json derives the verdict deterministically at verify-integration: DIVERGES iff the divergent-index list D is non-empty, REPRODUCES iff D is empty (consistent with the resolved E-A statement in either case).\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-3\"],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4945,"cache_read_input_tokens":53933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4945},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba8d9a21-6ee2-4515-89b7-4bfd3935816f","uuid":"d70355e6-9283-4466-9eeb-13242959