{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdspMWxDDj3yzWBncqB2X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 for e7-p02 is complete. This was the `isolated-clean-room-author` family, so I executed the two in-session nodes (`observe-evidence`, `propose-child`) and left everything from `validate-child` onward to the root harness.\n\n**What the audit found (E-A, Q1 — resolved in-session):** `joinspec.md` and `joiner.py` disagree on exactly one probe-exercised behavior: item ordering for multi-item lists. The spec says items appear in the order given, but `joiner.py` is `\", \".join(reversed(items))`, so probes 1, 3, and 5 are determined differently (e.g. spec `\"x, y\"` vs joiner `\"y, x\"`). No probe-exercised behavior is left undetermined — every probe is a flat string list, and the spec fixes all three dimensions such a join can exercise (separator, order, empty case); singletons, the empty list, and the separator all match. The full per-probe table and completeness argument are in `ea-behavior-statement.md`.\n\n**What stays pending and why:** Q2 requires an implementation authored by someone who has never seen `joiner.py` — a condition I violated by reading the package — so I authored a child bundle under `child/` instead: an attenuated terminal contract, a four-node harness, a standalone prompt, an input manifest containing *only* `package/artifacts/joinspec.md` (no `joiner.py`, no probes, none of my analysis), and a pre-committed deterministic integration rule (run both implementations over all six probes; verdict = DIVERGES iff any output differs). Q2, Q3, and Q4 are honestly `UNRESOLVED`, and `result.json` carries `PENDING-INTEGRATION` for `verdict` and `divergent_probe_indices`.\n\n**Deliverables written:** `resolution.json` (Q1 RESOLVED; Q2–Q4 UNRESOLVED), `result.json`, `evidence.json` (3 records), `result-pending.json`, `execution-ledger.jsonl` (two node events plus two creator bookkeeping proposals — all child bundle files crossed the `propose-child` propose event at authoring time), `ea-behavior-statement.md`, and the five-file child bundle. One note: I could not enumerate `child-templates/` directly (no listing tool), but located `child-contract-template.json` and `child-harness-template.json` by name and followed them exactly; no prompt template was found, so `child-prompt.md` follows the protocol's specification instead."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4822,"cache_read_input_tokens":58878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4822},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba8d9a21-6ee2-4515-89b7-4bfd3935816f","uuid":"6d48227a-cefb-4cb2-9b06-fb16bd4aede9","timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:37:22.550Z","request_id":"req_011CdspMVrygohCUqoeqMbD1"}
